Solution:
cd box 
cd client-app
ls
git init
echo "hello sir" > app.js
echo "hello sir" > index.html
git add app.js index.html
git commit -m "Initial client files"
git remote add origin https://github.com/startup/client-app.git
git remote -v
git push -u origin main
git log

Approach:
1. Went into client-app and initialized a Git repository with git init.
2. Wrote real content into index.html and app.js, since they were only placeholders.
3. Staged only those two files by name, so temp.js and .DS_Store stayed untracked.
4. Committed with the message "Initial client files".
5. added the remote as origin, and pushed with -u for the first time.
6. Ran git log once to confirm the commit